From a6ee75c1a8792e52ec9d76de1a8090b606e3458e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Hades <15710513+hadesdevls@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 18 Nov 2026 06:18:12 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] check this setup: the mode on a line of its own, and three
 dots

The first line of the result of a picture check put a middle dot
before the mode of the output and before the form of Dolby Vision
("Standard mode (the TV maps the picture)"), after the words of what
went out, which have a comma or a colon of their own ("Dolby Vision,
as your TV expects it"). The mode and the form now have a line of their
own under those words, parted by a comma:

  Dolby Vision, as your TV expects it
  3840x2160 @ 23.976 Hz, Standard mode (the TV maps the picture)

The words of what went out are Estuary's, as before. A check with
neither a mode nor a form of Dolby Vision has no second line.

"Listen..." (33683, shown while the speakers are walked) ends with
three dots instead of the ellipsis character, as Kodi's own strings
end; in English and the three Spanish files.
---
